{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/425393-vampire-the-requiem-legacy-of-kain","id":425393,"title":"Vampire: the Requiem + Legacy of Kain","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-02T10:25:08-08:00","id":425393,"title":"Vampire: the Requiem + Legacy of Kain","content":"Alright, mentioned in my Psychokinesis thread, I'm working on a hack for Legacy of Kain-esque vampires. \\(The link to my rough draft is in my sig) Which have more of a theme of transformation. The main thrust of it, includes the Mutation system, and how the Humanity system interacts with it. So here's some of my thoughts on it.<br /> <br /> First of all, Clans and Clan Banes. Should clans have them? I'm thinking yes. I don't know if they'll come out looking like B&amp;S Banes, being tied to Humanity and all, but they should. Another thing is, my home game-world uses a mix between Masquerade, VtR, and LoK vampires. In doing so, I've included the Salubim. A Kainified Salubri. I should probably wall the home stuff away from the 'canon' LoK stuff, but I'm not exactly sure I'll get to that.<br /> <br /> Secondly, Metamorphosis and pupation. Vampires don't get mutation unless they go into Pupate. My thoughts on this is they need to have a full blood bool, and hunker down for Torpor. They activate Pupate and the blood weaves a 'cocoon' around them, the look depends on Clan really, and the Vitae is used changing their form permanently. Now, Pupation is voluntary, to an extent. You can rack up three or so Blood Potency, and then Pupate and come out looking like a monster. Along with this, I'm thinking undertaking Pupation should be a Breaking Point against Humanity. <br /> <br /> Which brings me to Humanity, I'll probably get rid of Draugr, since LoK never hinted to inhuman vampires being mindless. Well, Turel was definitely inhuman, and nearly mindless until Raziel met him... But still. I'm on the fence if a cosmetic change should be a SECOND Breaking Point. Perhaps lower than Pupation. (Pupation is a Breaking Point 5 maybe? A Cosmetic Mutation Breaking Point at Humanity 2?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T11:19:00-08:00","id":425438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/425393-vampire-the-requiem-legacy-of-kain#post425393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all, Clans and Clan Banes. Should clans have them? I'm thinking yes. I don't know if they'll come out looking like B&amp;S Banes, being tied to Humanity and all, but they should. Another thing is, my home game-world uses a mix between Masquerade, VtR, and LoK vampires. In doing so, I've included the Salubim. A Kainified Salubri. I should probably wall the home stuff away from the 'canon' LoK stuff, but I'm not exactly sure I'll get to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, i'll start showing my ignorance (love LoK, but i have only played LoK2 so... i'll lack a lot of information , i'm sure of it. Be gentle with me :P): I had always thought that all vampires were clanless in LoK, being Vorador spawn and all that (not taking into account the Old ones). Besides, the Banes are already the Glyph energy, the bloodlust, and the impossibility of walking in daylight or in large water bodies, and those are the same to every vampire, right? So... not sure i'll add more Banes. If you feel like it, well, i'm sure you will be able to find some flavorful ones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/425393-vampire-the-requiem-legacy-of-kain#post425393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secondly, Metamorphosis and pupation. Vampires don't get mutation unless they go into Pupate. My thoughts on this is they need to have a full blood bool, and hunker down for Torpor. They activate Pupate and the blood weaves a 'cocoon' around them, the look depends on Clan really, and the Vitae is used changing their form permanently. Now, Pupation is voluntary, to an extent. You can rack up three or so Blood Potency, and then Pupate and come out looking like a monster. Along with this, I'm thinking undertaking Pupation should be a Breaking Point against Humanity.Which brings me to Humanity, I'll probably get rid of Draugr, since LoK never hinted to inhuman vampires being mindless. Well, Turel was definitely inhuman, and nearly mindless until Raziel met him... But still. I'm on the fence if a cosmetic change should be a SECOND Breaking Point. Perhaps lower than Pupation. (Pupation is a Breaking Point 5 maybe? A Cosmetic Mutation Breaking Point at Humanity 2?)</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with your ideas. However, i would make a Cosmetic Mutation a Humanity 7 Breaking Point, and Pupation Humanity 6 Breaking Point. They are HUGE points to mark that you're not human anymore, not by a long shot. And because of this, i would make them happen quickly. Besides, if they are no more Draugr (which i approve, given the game play style), the Breaking Points are even more dedicated to paint the character and colour their evolution, so no big problem there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T11:28:57-08:00","id":425445,"title":"","content":"Not exactly, the time of LoK2 is ill-defined about how each vampire works, but, after LoK2 Kain becomes Ascendant and spawns seven clans, who each have their own weaknesses and strengths. Since they are called Clans, and work like clans, making them clans is probably the best fit. amechra went ahead and did their Discipline spread, which I think are wonderful. My own campaign includes more clans, and I've gone ahead and done a sample (the Salubim). <br /> <br /> Yeah, I was thinking that they'd be huge marks to say that you are Inhuman, but 7 and 6 seem to high for me. Perhaps 5 and 4 respectively?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T11:43:43-08:00","id":425461,"title":"","content":"All of the non-Elder (i.e. other than the Lieutenants and Kain) Vampires were pretty much just beasts after they degenerated. Some of the fluff for <i>Nosgoth</i> indicated that Pupation leaves you <i>hungry</i>, and that you mentally degenerate if you aren't fed. They were infected with the madness of the Pillar Guardians through Kain, so Draugr are actually in theme.<br /> <br /> I'd say Pupating and then <i>not</i> eating is a Humanity breaking point. I'd also go with just fleshing out some more options for Protean \u2022\u2022 and \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 and <i>physical</i> mutations instead of Banes for lost Humanity. In my quick Clan write-ups, I set up Animalism, Auspex, Celerity, Protean, Resilience, and Vigor as being Disciplines <i>anyone</i> can take, so having Pupating be a way of applying permanent Predatory Aspects might be interested (the Zephonim, for example, would pick up Wall Crawling, while Rahabim would pick up Aquatic and Razelim would pick up Patagia). They would be picked out by Clan, and you could do it without actually <i>having</i> two dots of Protean.<br /> <br /> Do it in two steps, with the first &quot;evolving&quot; into the second, might be interesting. Let them keep both, if you'd like.<br /> <br /> Hell, have it stack with the ones you can normally get from the Discipline.<br /> <br /> So...<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><b>Dumahim:</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32996-protean-custom-options?p=40052#post40052\">Tough Hide</a> \u2192 Armor Plating</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><b>Melcahim:</b> Tremorsense \u2192 Hooked Hands</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><b>Rahabim: </b>Aquatic \u2192 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/66970-walking-shadows-mara-nicor?p=66973#post66973\">Shark's Grace</a></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><b>Razelim: </b>Patagia \u2192 Wings</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><b>Turelim:</b> Feral Senses \u2192 Horrid Claws<br /> <b>Zephonim:</b> Wall Crawling \u2192 Barbed Hands</span></span><br /> <br /> Or something.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T12:01:00-08:00","id":425502,"title":"","content":"I've set up a general purpose Mutation system. It's a bit like Preatory Aspects, but bought with dots received. It has Cosmetic Mutations (ones that appear, with a number you have to take) and Beneficial Mutations which are extra toppings of power, that can be like improved claws/fangs, giant size, starting a Bloodline/splitting off to a Clan. Where I'd have Protean's Predatory Aspects be a way to get other mutations. As for Pupation, it's voluntary to a point, go into Torpor with a full blood pool, come out with 1 or 2 left, and with the amount of Mutation your Blood Potency suggests. <br /> <br /> As of right now, I have it tied to Blood Potency, because as far as I can tell, Pupation comes with age and power, not loss of Humanity. However, that could be semantic. But I thought of removing Dragr, because even the most inhuman vampires didn't fit the profile of a Draugr. However, your two step clan one is... elegant. I'm going to have to think on this. (Have you looked up the system I have so far? Because, it seems even without the Clans Vampires evolve. Look at Vorador, he had the ancient's claws, green skin and bat ears. He was not a progeny of Kain. It seems Nuprator's curse is the extent at which his progeny devolve, instead of continuing to evolve. So maybe... Nuprator's curse is Humanity, hm?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T22:25:57-08:00","id":426208,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>PUPATION </b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Inhumanity. Monsters. Vampires are forever changed from when they were people. Their first nights highlight this fact, but hoary old monsters almost never look completely human, and some of them barely look human. The process of the vampire's evolution is called 'Pupation'. When a vampire is fat on blood, and it's blood starts to run thick, there is a longing to go into the deep-sleep of Torpor. They feed to the brink and lay down for slumber, and the blood spins into sickly cocoons. Within the vampire changes permanently. Pupation lasts for the duration of Torpor, At the end of the Pupation the vampire is drained to 1/2 Blood Potency (min. 1) Vitae. The vital essence and blood going to the greater transformation of the vampire.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">System here.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Thing is, I think one should tie devolutions to Humanity, like Banes, but evolutions to Blood Potency. Vampires evolve, that is... uh, natural. But Kain's brood went beyond, they kept getting more Beastial, picking up undesirable traits along the way. sometimes their mind went a little mad. I think that may be a better way than Draugr hood. Sometimes an Elder just picks up... a psychosis or two.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Also, on another note, the Strix work perfectly for the disembodied specters of the Hylden.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T03:40:48-08:00","id":427563,"title":"","content":"Alright. Started on the Clans and am MOSTLY done with the Mutations system. (Pulling heavily from Demon and Protean.) I am however, stumped on the Clan Bane and whether I should include a small list of needed Mutations. For the Banes, the obvious one that comes to mind is the Zephonim's weakness in the fact that they continually rot. I'm not sure how to model that. Every (Humanity) days they get a -1 to Social rolls until they make a crafts roll (or have it done for them) to replace their flesh/skin?<br /> <br /> <b>Turelim</b><br /> The Turelim vampires were progeny of Turel, who personally raised his clan during the over the century following the Raising of the lieutenants at the Tomb of the Sarafan. Alongside the Dumahim, Melchahim, Rahabim, Razielim, and Zephonim, it was one of the &quot;six legions of vampires&quot; involved in &quot;the destruction of the major human Kingdoms&quot;; pillaging Nosgoth, they had thoroughly domesticated humans within a hundred years, despite the efforts of the Vampire hunters. Turel's clan dominated an area in territory east of the Lake of the Dead and south-west of the Oracle's Cave. In the millennium after the raising of the lieutenants and establishment of Kain's empire, the &quot;lesser vampires&quot; provided &quot;amusement and spice to an increasingly uninspired court&quot;; and presumably the Turelim clan were involved in these internal struggles. The Council would help and foil plots between the clans, betting upon the outcome as the factions warred.<br /> <b>Nickname:</b> Tyrants<br /> <b>Clan Disciplines:</b> Auspex, <i>Psychokinesis</i>, Vigor<br /> <b>Clan Bane -:</b><br /> <b>Clan Mutations:</b> ???<br /> <b>Favored Attributes</b>: Strength or Wits<br /> <br /> All I've got done is the Turelim, so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T23:06:29-08:00","id":429889,"title":"","content":"UPDATE<br /> <br /> Got some docs from CLADVIS from rpg.net. from his attempt at converting LoK about 4 or 5 years ago. I don't agree with much of his choices, but he does good work. Wit his permission, I'm using some parts of it What's needed to be updated to Blood &amp; Smoke is, but I am a bit out of my league with the spirit rules, so any help with that? I'm not the best with Spirits, and beyond that, the systems haven't been updated to NWoD, they are still using <b>W:tO</b>.<br /> Other than that I have decided to do mandatory Clan mutations, I'm thinking 2 dots of Mutations for each. Razelim, for instance, will need to buy Wings 1 and 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}